      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The notion that governments will roll back climate regulations in the face of mass energy poverty or civil unrest is a far-fetched one, driven by a naive assumption that the public will always prioritize economic growth over environmental concerns. In reality, the public is increasingly aware of the climate crisis and is demanding action, even if it means higher energy costs in the short term. The transition to a low-carbon economy is inevitable, and the only question is how quickly and efficiently it can be achieved.",
      "source": "target",
